asr-000080
00:30:45.960 --> 00:30:51.440
Senator Joel Villanueva: Today, we examine whether the 2027 budget can deliver on that promise.

asr-000081
00:30:52.140 --> 00:30:54.560
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I was looking at the 2027 budget.

asr-000082
00:30:54.960 --> 00:31:10.360
Senator Joel Villanueva: The 2027 budget, CHED has proposed a budget of 35.453 billion, down by 12.916 billion or 26.7% from its 2026 level.

asr-000083
00:31:10.360 --> 00:31:24.360
Senator Joel Villanueva: The proposed obligation budget for our state universities and colleges is 141.090 billion, again lower by 2.979 billion or 2.1%.

asr-000084
00:31:24.960 --> 00:31:28.360
Senator Joel Villanueva: than the current budget.

asr-000085
00:31:28.360 --> 00:31:34.880
Senator Joel Villanueva: Parang hindi kagad maganda yung panimulang sinasabi ko sa nakikita kong mga numero.

asr-000086
00:31:35.240 --> 00:31:44.960
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ngunit nais po nating tiyakin na, bagamat ganito ang budget sa susunod na taon ay tunay nga pong magpapataas ng kalidad ng edukasyon at magpapalawak.

asr-000087
00:31:46.120 --> 00:31:48.600
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang access ito sa ating mga kabataan.

asr-000088
00:31:48.600 --> 00:31:54.600
Senator Joel Villanueva: The allocation for universal access to quality tertiary education again falls down from 37.547 billion

asr-000089
00:31:54.960 --> 00:32:04.380
Senator Joel Villanueva: to 27.790 billion, or a reduction of 9.757 billion.

asr-000090
00:32:05.060 --> 00:32:06.900
Senator Joel Villanueva: Talagang importante ang edukasyon.

asr-000091
00:32:08.160 --> 00:32:15.640
Senator Joel Villanueva: We must also prepare for the implementation, of course, of RA 12325,

asr-000092
00:32:15.780 --> 00:32:19.380
Senator Joel Villanueva: Enhancing the Universal Access to Quality Tertiary Education Act,

asr-000093
00:32:19.380 --> 00:32:25.380
Senator Joel Villanueva: which we, again, authored, sponsored, co-sponsored.

asr-000094
00:32:26.820 --> 00:32:36.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: Only 12.6% of tertiary education subsidy grantees in the first semester of academic year 2025-2026

asr-000095
00:32:36.140 --> 00:32:38.500
Senator Joel Villanueva: came from four-piece households.

asr-000096
00:32:39.480 --> 00:32:45.980
Senator Joel Villanueva: The reform is intended to better direct tertiary education assistance toward disadvantaged learners.

asr-000097
00:32:45.980 --> 00:32:49.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: There are positive movements naman.

asr-000098
00:32:49.140 --> 00:32:52.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: We look at the Student Financial Assistance Programs.

asr-000099
00:32:52.140 --> 00:33:02.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: It increased from 2.154 billion to 3.185 billion, or almost 48%,

asr-000100
00:33:02.140 --> 00:33:11.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: with beneficiaries increasing from 42,128 to 49,243.

asr-000101
00:33:11.140 --> 00:33:14.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: Now, the Medical Scholarship and Return Service Program,

asr-000102
00:33:14.140 --> 00:33:17.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: which is also very close to this representation's heart,

asr-000103
00:33:17.140 --> 00:33:18.580
Senator Joel Villanueva: increases to

asr-000104
00:33:18.580 --> 00:33:21.560
Senator Joel Villanueva: 1.232 billion.

asr-000109
00:33:22.900 --> 00:33:25.600
Senator Joel Villanueva: But I was looking at the beneficiaries,

asr-000110
00:33:25.600 --> 00:33:28.100
Senator Joel Villanueva: parang yung target ay mas mababa,

asr-000111
00:33:28.100 --> 00:33:29.520
Senator Joel Villanueva: but we'll go to that later on.

asr-000117
00:33:30.020 --> 00:33:51.800
Senator Joel Villanueva: We also cannot discuss the UP budget without discussing the Philippine General Hospital, and that's why Dr. Gap is here. Its hospital services program is proposed at 7.291 billion, lower by 805.457 million or 9.9%.

asr-000118
00:33:51.820 --> 00:34:04.780
Senator Joel Villanueva: The budget retains 800 million for zero balance billing and provides 576.522 million for medicines under the medical assistance for indigent patients.

asr-000119
00:34:05.680 --> 00:34:20.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: We need to know again if these amounts are sufficient to protect poor patients who depend on PGH and thank God, before I continue, let me acknowledge our Chairperson of the Senate Committee on Finance.

asr-000120
00:34:20.300 --> 00:34:21.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I think...

asr-000121
00:34:21.820 --> 00:34:25.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: He deserves a round of applause for all of us.

asr-000122
00:34:26.360 --> 00:34:34.260
Senator Joel Villanueva: Considering what I have already stated, hindi rin po dapat maiwan ang ating mga manggagawa across our SUCs.

asr-000123
00:34:34.420 --> 00:34:45.860
Senator Joel Villanueva: You're looking at 18,436 permanent positions remain unfilled while CHED has 1,097 job order and contract of service personnel.

asr-000124
00:34:45.860 --> 00:34:51.680
Senator Joel Villanueva: Hindi naman po pwedeng lumawak ang serbisyong pang edukasyon habang nahiiwan po.

asr-000125
00:34:51.820 --> 00:34:53.520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang mga manggagawang naghahatid nito.

asr-000126
00:34:54.020 --> 00:34:59.600
Senator Joel Villanueva: Magtatapos ako kasi gusto kong masimulan na natin ang ating pagdinig.

asr-000127
00:35:00.200 --> 00:35:03.820
Senator Joel Villanueva: Simple lang po ang ating sukatan sa dulo ng lahat ng ito.

asr-000128
00:35:04.760 --> 00:35:09.620
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kung libre po ang kolehyo sa estudyante, dapat hindi po kapos ang paaralan.

asr-000129
00:35:10.360 --> 00:35:16.020
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kung may scholarship or subsidy, dapat naman makarating ito sa higit na nangangailangan.

asr-000130
00:35:16.020 --> 00:35:21.380
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang budget po na ito ay tungkol sa pagbibigay ng pagkakataon sa kabataang Pilipino.

asr-000131
00:35:21.820 --> 00:35:23.940
Senator Joel Villanueva: At makapagtapos ng kanyang pag-aaral.

asr-000132
00:35:24.480 --> 00:35:30.360
Senator Joel Villanueva: At sa pagtiyak na may sapat na suporta ang mga institusyon at manggagawang tumutulong po sa kanila.

asr-000133
00:35:30.800 --> 00:35:37.960
Senator Joel Villanueva: And so with that, we now proceed with the budget briefing of CHED and the SUCs.

asr-000134
00:35:38.560 --> 00:35:40.640
Senator Joel Villanueva: Marami pong salamat muli sa inyong pagdalo.

asr-000135
00:35:40.640 --> 00:35:48.100
